<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phasis (town)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phasis was an ancient Greek colony on the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast, founded by settlers from Miletus in the 6th century BCE near the mouth of the Phasis river (Rioni), close to modern Poti in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. It was the main port of Colchis, linking the Greek world with the river route into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, and later a Roman and Byzantine fortress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phasis-town.jpg" alt="Phasis (town)" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samuel Butler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colchis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Iberia lay on a trade route that ran from the Black Sea up the <b>Phasis</b> (Rioni) river through Colchis and over the Likhi range, then down the Mtkvari towards Albania and the Caspian, and it traded with the Greek cities of the Black Sea, with Armenia and with…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-iberia">Kingdom of Iberia · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
